      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You have the right idea about needing something to avoid the accidental clicking, but instead of a lock feature it should be simpler to implement a confirmation dialogue. Confirmation dialogues should be standard with destructive actions. They put them in for some actions but we all know the UI is not finalised so this request may have to wait until we see what they do with the new UI.",
